  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LMI Research and Educational Networks (RENS) Training</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This workshop for the Lower Mekong nations has three focus areas: 1) forming and enhancing science and education collaborations among US scientists and scientists of the countries of the LMR; 2)developing human capacity to operate and maintain cyberinfrastructure in support of science and engineering collaborations; 3) policy, funding and regulatory best practices in cyberinfrastructure development and science collaboration. .The workshop will bring together operators and managers of Research and Education Networks (RENs) at the campus and national levels; researchers from institutions within the region and from the US who collaborate in three main areas of science and engineering: disaster management, climate change and forestry; and policy-makers and leaders from government and academia involved in supporting the development of cyberinfrastructure and collaborative science in their countries and in the region. .</narrative>
  </description>
